nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T18:17:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T18:17:04Z","body":"Thanks @hpvb for looking into this!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2672312832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676093396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103077#issuecomment-2676093396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103077","id":2676093396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgfHU","user":{"login":"wildlachs","id":105976809,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlET6Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105976809?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs","html_url":"https://github.com/wildlachs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wildlachs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T08:38:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T08:38:06Z","body":"I think this broke my build pipeline.\r\n\r\nThis is how I build my windows production build:\r\n```\r\n# Windows production build\r\nscons platform=windows \\\r\n    target=template_release \\\r\n    arch=x86_64 \\\r\n    use_llvm=yes \\\r\n    linker=mold \\\r\n    precision=double \\\r\n    production=yes \\\r\n    scu_build=yes \\\r\n    scu_limit=1024 \\\r\n    optimize=speed\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsing MinGW64 running on Fedora 41:\r\n```\r\n$ x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc --version\r\nx86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc (GCC) 14.2.1 20240801 (Fedora MinGW 14.2.1-3.fc41)\r\nCopyright (C) 2024 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\r\nThis is free software; see the source for copying conditions.  There is NO\r\nwarranty; not even for MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput of build process:\r\n```\r\nscons: Reading SConscript files ...\r\nAuto-detected 12 CPU cores available for build parallelism. Using 11 cores by default. You can override it with the `-j` or `num_jobs` arguments.\r\nSCU: Generating build files... (max includes per SCU: 1024)\r\nUsing MinGW, arch x86_64\r\nBuilding for platform \"windows\", architecture \"x86_64\", target \"template_release\".\r\nUsing LTO: full\r\nChecking for C header file mntent.h... (cached) no\r\nscons: done reading SConscript files.\r\nscons: Building targets ...\r\n[ 75%] Compiling scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.cpp ...\r\n[ 77%] Compiling scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.cpp ...\r\n[ 94%] /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-w64-mingw32/14.2.1/../../../../x86_64-w64-mingw32/bin/as: scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: too many sections (38865)\r\n/tmp/ccyyzFXX.s: Assembler messages:\r\n/tmp/ccyyzFXX.s: Fatal error: can't write 1 byte to section .text of scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: 'file too big'\r\n/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-w64-mingw32/14.2.1/../../../../x86_64-w64-mingw32/bin/as: scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: too many sections (38865)\r\n/tmp/ccyyzFXX.s: Fatal error: scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: file too big\r\nscons: *** [scene/gui/scu/scu_scene_gui.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o] Error 1\r\n/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-w64-mingw32/14.2.1/../../../../x86_64-w64-mingw32/bin/as: scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: too many sections (56069)\r\n/tmp/ccwG5nE5.s: Assembler messages:\r\n/tmp/ccwG5nE5.s: Fatal error: can't write 7 bytes to section .text of scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: 'file too big'\r\n/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-w64-mingw32/14.2.1/../../../../x86_64-w64-mingw32/bin/as: scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: too many sections (56069)\r\n/tmp/ccwG5nE5.s: Fatal error: scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o: file too big\r\nscons: *** [scene/resources/scu/scu_scene_resources.gen.windows.template_release.double.x86_64.o] Error 1\r\nscons: building terminated because of errors.\r\nINFO: Time elapsed: 00:01:56.52\r\n```\r\n\r\nI am using an scu build with maximum limit because I hope the compiler is able to perform the maximal level of optimization this way. With beta4 it worked, but now it's throwing \"file too big\" errors.\r\n\r\nWhen I build with the same settings, but without scu enabled, everything builds fine.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676093396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2685675135","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103077#issuecomment-2685675135","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103077","id":2685675135,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gFCZ_","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T17:05:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T17:05:01Z","body":"@wildlachs The current LTO settings will already try to analyze the whole program. Adding SCU on top of that should not give the compiler additional information. I think you should consider LTO and SCU to be different systems to get to the same end-result.\r\n\r\nUsing SCU together with LTO is basically \"doubling up\".","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2685675135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6191266305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103077#issuecomment-6191266305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103077","id":6191266305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcQc6AQ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T11:44:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T11:44:58Z","body":"For the record, I did some tests to revert this workaround with GCC 16, but I could reproduce a broken mingw-gcc LTO build (no linking error, but the build was smaller than expected and a number of symbols were missing). I haven't managed to re-reproduce it, but so the flakiness is still there without those flags.\r\n\r\nIt's worth noting that by testing removing these flags, the Windows `template_release` became 12.4 MiB smaller, so there's definitely a size cost to this workaround.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6191266305/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]